WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:06.120
The alcoholic, dimension-hopping mad scientist
Rick Sanchez could be called a lot of things.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.690
"Compassionate," "friendly," and "filled with
basic human decency" are not among them.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.179
"Hey, Jerry, don't worry about it.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.650
So what if the most meaningful day of your
life was a simulation operating at minimum

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:17.010
capacity?"

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:22.110
Over two seasons, Rick and Morty have killed
countless people, destroyed whole civilizations,

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.200
and just made some pretty terrible life decisions.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.820
Here are some of the worst things Rick and
Morty have ever done.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.869
Murdered a bunch of bureaucrats

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:35.219
Rick's brazen disregard for most everything
is established in the pilot, when he drags

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:41.309
Morty out of class for an expedition to Dimension
35C so Rick can use him to smuggle some powerful

00:00:41.309 --> 00:00:43.510
Mega Seeds through interdimensional customs.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:46.819
"And I'm gonna need you to put them waaaay
up inside your butthole, Morty."

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:47.819
"My butt?"

00:00:47.819 --> 00:00:50.079
"Put them way up inside there, as far as they
can fit!"

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:51.079
"Oh geez, Rick."

00:00:51.079 --> 00:00:56.069
But their plan doesn't work out, so Rick has
to commandeer a portal home while Morty engages

00:00:56.069 --> 00:00:58.699
in a shootout with the customs officials.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.120
Morty ends up killing dozens of aliens with
personal lives and loving families.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:04.600
"They're not robots, Rick!"

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.900
"It's a figure of speech, Morty!

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:06.900
They're bureaucrats.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.900
I don't respect them."

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.440
Blew up the Zigerions

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.241
Kidnapping people isn't the nicest way to
get secrets, but you can't help but like the

00:01:14.241 --> 00:01:17.280
Zigerions in Episode 4 of the first season.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.820
After a series of simulations within simulations,
the alien scammers maneuver Rick into a situation

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.960
where he gives up the recipe for concentrated
dark matter…

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.280
"Grab that bucket!

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:30.530
OK, two parts plutonic quarks, one part cesium."

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.149
...but as usual, Rick is one step ahead of
them the whole time.

00:01:34.149 --> 00:01:38.259
The Zigerions try out the recipe… and blow
up their entire ship.

00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:42.310
Which would have been bad enough, but of course
the show adds this little tidbit right before

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.310
they all die:

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.609
"And listen, I'm sorry for yelling earlier.

00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:48.770
I couldn't ask for a better staff.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.439
I love you guys!

00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:52.009
And I love all your families."

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:56.490
Man, it's like Rick can only destroy things
with families.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.700
Cronenberged the world

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.770
Rick's done some pretty bad things, but leaving
an entire reality in the grip of horrible

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.979
suffering might be one of the worst.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:09.899
After inadvertently making the entire population
of Earth fall violently in love with Morty,

00:02:09.899 --> 00:02:11.860
Rick fixes the problem with a little science.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.400
"What are we gonna do, Rick?!"

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.940
"We're gonna be fine, Morty, relax.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.230
I whipped up an anecdote.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.450
It's based on praying mantis DNA."

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.360
When that turns everyone into bug-monsters,
Rick fixes the problem with better science.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:29.060
"It's koala, mixed with rattlesnake, chimpanzee,
cactus, shark, golden retriever and just a

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.400
smidge of dinosaur.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.370
Should add up to normal humanity."

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.569
That's when the episode gets dark.

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:39.090
Rick's new serum also backfires, but do Rick
and Morty stick around to fix things?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.090
Nope!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.040
They just abandon everyone in the world to
a lifetime of suffering and take the places

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.670
of their dead selves in an alternate reality.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:46.660
"Rick!

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.240
What about the reality we left behind?!"

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:51.620
"What about the reality where Hitler cured
cancer, Morty?

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.989
The answer is 'don't think about it.'"

00:02:53.989 --> 00:02:55.799
Created Abradolf Lincler

00:02:55.799 --> 00:03:00.610
The first season finale introduced a ton of
new awesome characters, like Bird Person and

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.610
Squanchy.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.290
"Is there a good place for me to squanch around
here?"

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.900
"Squanchy, you can squanch wherever you want
to, man!

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:07.980
Mi casa es su casa, dawg!"

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:08.980
"Alright!"

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:14.400
But the strangest guest at the party has to
be Abradolf Lincler, a mutant creation with

00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:19.920
the combined DNA of Abraham Lincoln and Adolf
Hitler who was abandoned by his father-slash-god,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.990
Rick.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:25.969
The existential pain of this guy is just off
the charts, and Rick, being Rick, couldn't

00:03:25.969 --> 00:03:26.969
care less.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:30.930
Even when Abradolf Lincler sacrifices himself
and things get emotional and people start

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.220
crying, Rick's only got one thing to say:

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.560
"But at least he didn't die in vain.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.820
He got these crystals.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.319
And these babies just saved this lame-ass
party!

00:03:42.319 --> 00:03:43.319
Wubba-lubba-dub-dub!"

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:47.599
Because there's nothing like sacrifice and
emotional torment to kick off a party, right?

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:49.010
Abandoned Jerry forever

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.079
The Cronenberg episode left the original version
of Jerry in a mutated hellhole, but Rick wasn't

00:03:54.079 --> 00:03:55.140
done with the guy.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.849
In season 2, episode 2, Rick drops him off
at a facility that basically amounts to a

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:01.840
giant daycare for Jerrys.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:06.680
Dozens of versions of Jerry wander around
in various states of confusion and distraction,

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.989
waiting to be picked up again.

00:04:07.989 --> 00:04:12.340
But one room contains all the Jerrys who were
completely abandoned by their Ricks and Mortys.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.920
"These are the Jerrys whose Ricks and Mortys
never came back."

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.070
These guys are stuck in a nursing home on
an alien planet.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.070
Forever.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:26.690
Talk about depressing.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.890
Created and destroyed a universe

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:33.700
Rick's got a pretty heavy god vibe going throughout
the series, and nowhere is that more apparent

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.080
than in his choice of car battery — which
contains an entire universe whose sole purpose

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.280
is to...well, power his car.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.650
"You have a whole planet sitting around making
power for you?!

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:44.650
That's slavery!"

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:45.650
"That's society!

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.170
They work for each other, Morty."

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:51.500
Basically, Rick's car battery contains an
entire civilization of sentient, intelligent

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:55.970
beings… who happen to be so intelligent
they make another battery with its own micro

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:56.970
universe.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:01.950
And Rick has zero problems smashing that battery
to pieces, killing the civilization inside.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.700
"Oh, hey guys.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:08.140
I just finished cooking us a feast!"

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.650
"You monster!"

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:14.560
Yup, that's all of these guys, and their families,
smashed out of existence.

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.440
By the time Rick and Morty escape the car
battery, all the creatures inside know that

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.310
they're slaves...and they have no choice but
to keep their meaningless existence going.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:26.280
"One of two things was gonna happen: I was
gonna have to toss a broken battery.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.080
Or the battery wouldn't be broken."

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.060
Is this guy the worst yet?

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:33.400
Almost...but there's more.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.800
Because there was also the time Rick and Morty...

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.720
Slaughtered innocent aliens

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:42.170
In season two's penultimate episode, Rick
and Morty stop for windshield wiper fluid

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:44.700
on a planet which is about to commence "The
Festival."

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.080
"You've been able to sustain world peace because
you have one night a year where you all run

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.180
around robbing and murdering each other without
consequence!"

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.180
"That's right!"

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.180
"What?!"

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.180
"It's like The Purge, Morty!

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.190
Th-That movie, The Purge!"

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:59.170
Rick convinces Morty to stick around and watch
the Purge, and they try to save a girl, and

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.780
it all backfires when they get caught up in
the middle of the mayhem.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:03.600
"It's the hardest-working liver in the galaxy,
Morty.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.050
Now it has a hole in it.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.400
I hope it was worth it."

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:07.400
"I was just trying to do right!"

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.960
"Yeah, well that's not really the theme of
tonight's party.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.290
Heads up."

00:06:11.290 --> 00:06:16.080
In the end, they strap on a pair of powered
battle suits and go to town on the townsfolk,

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.480
killing just about everyone.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.170
"You're really going for it over there.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:23.190
I, uh, think, uh, I think those people were
just hiding."

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.400
"I don't give a s---!"

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.380
Put deadly bacteria in ice cream

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.490
If there's anything Rick cares about, it definitely
isn't Jerry.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.961
And we got solid proof of that in season two's
eighth episode, which opens with Jerry in

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.660
an alien hospital, projectile-spewing toxic
vomit.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.860
"Watch out for that stuff.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:42.120
It'll stain if it gets on your clothes, and
it'll send you on a murderous rage if it gets

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.120
in your eyes or mouth."

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:47.770
...which happened because Rick stored some
mutant bacteria in a pint of Cherry Garcia

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:48.800
ice cream.

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.050
And because of that, Jerry comes close to
getting castrated so his genitals can serve

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.270
as another guy's heart transplant.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.650
But in the end, as terrible a guy as Rick
may be, one thing's for sure: He always has

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.800
the situation under control.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.300
"Bwanuh-dun-nuh-nuh nuh nuhhhh.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:08.620
Bwah nuh, nuh-nuh-nuhhh."

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:09.320
Thanks for watching!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:12.180
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:14.410
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

